<p>A fire at a fairground in Villahermosa in southeastern Mexico killed at least five people, authorities said. The blaze erupted early on May 7 at the Parque Tabasco Dora María during the Tabasco Fair. The fire broke out during a concert attended by thousands; the BBC reported that about 135,000 people were at the event.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/qKZG0cO5tclS--GsJrCnnVCvIX3M7uK9BtyBxH7cPvgvcmUdvnm8LiZp7LUvsGHbz0ZrZfQBSRzoWFU3VOvfBSWcr1DkACHzzfk12GZY1_bDWyGTvub9Yd1zpgFS7aWp97GzQOQKdMwr7vSuimRYeMQxofCLQnTNWzsELGkIHXD9fTYvh5oovCfFiD3K97aA6JfkmZq7b_vi5OBEEc8vWsK3Xp_Qrp0' alt='The fire at the Tabasco Fair on May 6, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Stalls destroyed: Tabasco Gov. Javier May Rodríguez said flames swept through about 200 stalls in Nave 1 of the fairground.</li><li>Fire controlled: Emergency crews brought the fire under control, according to state authorities.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Tabasco Gov. Javier May Rodríguez: In social-media remarks cited by local reporting, May Rodríguez said the community would move forward together after the fire. (<a href='https://unomasuno.com.mx/nacional/incendio-en-feria-tabasco-cinco-muertos-y-perdidas-millonarias/'>unomásuno</a>)</li><li>Local authorities: Authorities said they had not determined the cause of the fire and that it remained under investigation. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/raging-fire-at-mexican-fairground-kills-five-authorities-say'>The Straits Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/5/7/huge-fire-at-mexican-fair-kills-five-people'>Huge fire at Mexican fair kills five people</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/raging-fire-at-mexican-fairground-kills-five-authorities-say'>Raging fire at Mexico fairground kills five, authorities say</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cq6py38q81ro'>Five killed in huge fire at packed Mexico fa